  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W S Darley and obligated $990M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. W S Darley and won 1,906 awards with an average award size of $520K, and obligations fell 33.3% year over year. W S Darley and received the vast majority of its obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $984M; the next-largest buyers were the General Services Administration with $4M and the Department of Justice with $2M. W S Darley and’s work clusters in a few NAICS markets: Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $517M and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $436M, followed by smaller totals in Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). This snapshot highlights buyer concentration, the primary industry markets, and the scale of awards so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are W S Darley and’s main federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is W S Darley and’s main federal customer, obligating $984M. The General Services Administration and the Department of Justice follow with $4M and $2M respectively. Smaller agency buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $248K and the Department of State at $42.7K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products generate W S Darley and’s federal sales?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is W S Darley and’s largest market at $517M, and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing is the next largest at $436M. W S Darley and also has obligations in Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing ($13.9M) and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing ($11M), plus several smaller NAICS categories."
      }
    ]
